# Bog Stalker — swamp T2 basic tank (HP 24, basic + limited powerful defend + limited powerful recover)

+title Bog Stalker
+image monsters/swamp_beast_4.png
+blood #2a4a3a
+stats hp=24

+move Attack
  narration: A thick-knuckled limb lashes out from the murk.
  narration: It lunges low, jaw splitting wider than it should.

+move Defend
  narration: It flattens against the bog, half-submerged, hide gone slick and stone-grey.

+move Recover
  narration: It sinks to the gill-line, drinking the rot back into itself.

+move Heavy Power Defend
  narration: It folds inward and lets the swamp rise around it — water, weed, bone-mat — armor of the place itself.

+move Heavy Power Recover
  narration: The water around it bubbles black and the wounds you've put in it close like seams pulled tight.

+intro
The reeds part without anything visibly parting them. Then a ridge breaks
the water, then a long flat head you mistook for a half-sunk log. The eyes
are old — older than they have any right to be, in something this size.
It does not hurry. The bog hurries for it.

+win
> gold 12
> tag killed_bog_stalker
It settles back into the water without a sound, going where it came from.
The swamp closes up over it and after a moment you couldn't say where it
had been.

+lose
You go down in the wet. The cold is the last thing you notice.
